<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    @* Declared here as well as in the stylesheet, because this is the earliest point
       a browser — or an extension deciding whether a site needs its help — can read
       it. AniQueue ships a full dark palette, so anything re-theming it on top is
       redoing work, and in one measured case broke the page outright (§9). *@
    <meta name="color-scheme" content="light dark" />
    @* Tells Dark Reader to leave this page alone, which is its documented opt-out
       for sites that already have a dark theme — and AniQueue does, immediately
       above and behind prefers-color-scheme in the stylesheet.

       This is not a preference about appearance. The extension's dynamic theme
       rewrites <head> while the page loads and then watches for changes, and that
       rewriting breaks Blazor's renderer: it holds live references to the nodes it
       created, so a node moved or removed underneath it fails the next render with
       "insertBefore … parentNode is null", then "No element is currently associated
       with component 1", and the circuit dies on load. Measured in both Firefox and
       Chromium, on this page, with nothing else installed (§9).

       In Dark Reader's own source this tag is checked before it does anything: with
       the lock present it never starts its theme or its watchers, so there is no
       mutation to lose a race against. Removing it re-enables an extension fighting
       a dark theme the application already has. *@
    <meta name="darkreader-lock" />
    <base href="/" />
    @* Without an explicit icon, browsers probe /favicon.ico on every page load.
       That 404s, and the 404 handler re-executes the whole app — returning a 4.6 KB
       HTML page in answer to a request for an icon. *@
    <link rel="icon" href="@Assets["favicon.svg"]" type="image/svg+xml" />
    <ResourcePreloader />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="@Assets["app.css"]" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="@Assets["AniQueue.Web.styles.css"]" />
    <ImportMap />
    <HeadOutlet @rendermode="InteractiveServer" />
</head>

<body>
    <Routes @rendermode="InteractiveServer" />
    <ReconnectModal />
    <script src="@Assets["_framework/blazor.web.js"]"></script>
</body>

</html>
